Z||000000||2M4 Dale||02-12-2000||01:54 PM||||doing a clutch job on my 87 coupe-4cly./5spd. ? I think that this job is probably over my head. I might want to rebuild the engine while it's out as well. Or maybe swap in a V6...If anyone is capable please respond to this thread or email me with $ quote. I would like to get started as soon as possible.  Thanks, Dale<P>P.S. I can work out a Hellava good gun deal for anyone interested in this job...If interested<p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 02-12-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sage||02-12-2000||03:24 PM||||I'm not really close enough to do you much good first hand, but I just wanted to pass on that the 2.5 is not that challenging to rebuild.  A stock set of hand tools and a torque wrench is about all you need.  There has to be someone around there that rebuilds engines.  Most of your investment will be in machine shop costs if you have to have anything major done.  Many parts houses carry standard rebuild kits.  You can get them that include just a gasket-bearing-rering kit or that include new pistons and even a cam&lifters. There are also places that sell crank kits which include a crank,rods and pistons.  I bought a kit from a place in Mich. (Fertig-Marsch I think) for $220.00; included complete gasket set, oversize pistons, timing set, new cam, lifters and oil pump.  You will be ahead to take the cradle out yourself, unless you want to caontract someone to do the whole job and then just write a check!  The v6 swap pretty much requires a donor car .  You have to change the ecm as well as the engine.  It can be done but probably not be cheap.  If you call around, I believe you will find a shop that won't laugh at you.  Use the phone, you are not that far from Akron-Canton area, there has to be some body around there that will take you seriously and not just "take you".  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||02-12-2000||05:44 PM||||Rebuilding the motor I'm sure I could do..Done a bunch of small block Chevys and a few Pontiac V8s. The basic problem I have is that I don't the place or the equipment to lift the Fiero body and remove the engine/trans-cradle assembly.||||reg||1
