Z||000005||wkayl||02-12-2000||09:26 PM||||Rebuilding the 2.5 isn't too tough (if I cam do it almost any one can).  I was driving my son's 84SE about a month after he got it and as I was climbing I-70 west of Denver a rod made it's presence known.  Biggest problem was cost(crank,cracked head,pitted cyl wall,pistons,cam,oil pump, etc.)  $1,000 later , and I did the labor, we had a great running car.  Too bad some idiot had to run a stop sign Jan 21st and wreck it. <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/crash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/crash.html</A> ||||reg||1
